# Web frontend

- Every mutation invalidates (or updates) every query whose data it changes.
- All API calls go through the typed client in `src/lib/api.ts`. No untyped `fetch` in components.
- Shared fixed values are `as const` tuples with a derived type.
- Every mutation shows success and error feedback.
- Use constrained inputs (select, radio) instead of free text when the values are fixed.
- Check UI changes in the browser without a manual reload.

## Good

```ts
export const CATEGORIES = ['billing', 'sales', 'support', 'unknown'] as const;
export type Category = (typeof CATEGORIES)[number];

useMutation({
  mutationFn: classifyRequest,
  onSuccess: () => queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['requests'] }),
});
```

## Bad

```tsx
useMutation({ mutationFn: classifyRequest }); // table stays stale, no feedback
<input placeholder="billing | sales | support | unknown" /> // free text for a fixed set
```
